I used to work as a UX Designer at Showrunner ... so here's the truth: 
their core engine isn’t magic. 
the core engine is just a finetuned LLM doing all the heavy lifting... No fancy pipelines, no secret sauce . .  it’s ridiculously simple, all the animations are predefined and made by motion designers

 Here’s a basic example of how it actually works:

{
  "character": {
    "name": "Elon",
    "facial_expression": "SKEPTICAL_RAISED_BROW", 
    "body_movement": "LEAN_FORWARD_SHIFT_WEIGHT",
    "dialog": "You really expect me to fuckin believe that?",
    "body_language": {
      "hands": "ONE_HAND_ON_HIP_OTHER_GESTURING"
    }
  }
}

and there is an agent called Time orchestrator who controls the events ridiculously simple too , I don't know how they outmarted amazon to invest in this crap !
